<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>FAQ | RGV Hackathon</title>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/global.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/partials.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/info.css">
</head>
<body>
    <%- include("./partials/navbar.ejs") %>

    <main class="info-page">
        <section class="info-header">
            <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
            <p>
                Find answers to common questions about RGV Hackathon.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="faq-section">
            <h2>General Information</h2>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What is RGV Hackathon?</h3>
                <p>
                    RGV Hackathon is an event where participants
                    collaborate to develop technology projects,
                    learn new skills, and connect with developers
                    throughout the Rio Grande Valley.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>When is the hackathon?</h3>
                <p>
                    RGV Hackathon takes place November 19–21, 2026.
                    The main 24-hour hackathon begins November 20
                    at 9:00 AM and ends November 21 at 9:00 AM.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Do I need programming experience?</h3>
                <p>
                    No. Participants of all experience levels
                    are welcome. Beginners can attend workshops
                    and collaborate with experienced developers.
                </p>
            </div>

            <h2>Registration and Teams</h2>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>How do I register?</h3>
                <p>
                    Create an account, navigate to the Events page,
                    and register for the hackathon event.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Do I need a team?</h3>
                <p>
                    Participants can create their own team or
                    apply to join an existing team through
                    the Teams page.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>How do I join a team?</h3>
                <p>
                    Visit the Teams page, select a team,
                    and submit a request to join.
                    A team member can approve your application.
                </p>
            </div>

            <h2>Projects and Activities</h2>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>How do I submit a project?</h3>
                <p>
                    Once you belong to a team, navigate to
                    My Project. Enter your project title,
                    description, and repository link to
                    submit your project.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Can I update my project submission?</h3>
                <p>
                    Yes. Team members can return to the
                    project page to edit their team's submission.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Are there workshops and other activities?</h3>
                <p>
                    Yes. RGV Hackathon features workshops,
                    networking opportunities, competitions,
                    and other activities throughout the event.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="info-footer">
            <h2>Still Have Questions?</h2>
            <p>
                Visit our Contact Us page for more information
                about RGV Hackathon.
            </p>

            <a href="/contact" class="info-button">
                Contact Us
            </a>
        </section>
    </main>

    <%- include("./partials/footer.ejs") %>
</body>
</html>
